serverLicense.detail:
Lantern's editor runs Microsoft's VS Code server on your machine. Microsoft requires you to accept its licence terms before it runs, so Lantern does not accept them for you.

In short: the server is free to use but is not open source; it is licensed for use with VS Code, and Microsoft may collect usage data as described in its terms. Read the full text at {url}

Your answer is kept for your user account. If you decline, the editor stays off and you can retry from the editor tab.
